  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>If using beef: heat the oil in the pan on medium-high and brown the cubes for <b>2–3 minutes</b>.</li><li>Pour the dashi into the pan and bring it to a boil. Hold a small sieve or ladle in the dashi, put the <b>doenjang</b> (and gochujang, if using) in it and press it through with a spoon until no lumps are left.</li><li>Add the potato and onion. Cover and simmer on <b>medium</b> for <b>6 minutes</b>.</li></ul>",
